https://arxiv.org/pdf/1606.01796, Scholze's q-analogues in 18 pages, MUST READ
    - (Page 1) Define the $q$-analogues of integers $[n]_q = \frac{q^n - 1}{q - 1} = 1 + q + \dots + q^{n-1}$, $q$-factorials $[n]_q! = \prod_{k=1}^n [k]_q$, and Gaussian $q$-binomial coefficients $\binom{n}{k}_q = \frac{[n]_q!}{[k]_q! [n-k]_q!}$.
    - (Page 1) Show that the $q$-binomial coefficient $\binom{n}{k}_q$ counts the number of $k$-dimensional subspaces of $\mathbb{F}_q^n$.
    - (Page 1) Define the Jackson $q$-derivative $D_q f(x) = \frac{f(qx) - f(x)}{qx - x}$, compute $D_q(x^n) = [n]_q x^{n-1}$, and verify that $\lim_{q \to 1} D_q f(x) = f'(x)$.
    - (Page 2) Formulate the $q$-de Rham complex $q\text{-}\Omega_{R/\mathbb{Z}}^\bullet$ over $\mathbb{Z}[[q-1]]$ specializing to de Rham cohomology at $q \to 1$.
    - (Page 2) Compute the $q$-de Rham complex for $R = \mathbb{Z}[x]$ using the Jackson $q$-derivative.
    - (Page 3) Relate the $q$-de Rham complex to the de Rham-Witt complex $W\Omega_{R/\mathbb{F}_p}^\bullet$ and crystalline cohomology.
    - (Page 4) Compare classical Betti-de Rham comparisons over $\mathbb{C}$ with $p$-adic comparisons between étale, crystalline, and de Rham cohomology.

https://arxiv.org/pdf/1003.1935, Langlands-Kottwitz for modular curves in 39 pages
    - Fix a prime $p$ and integer $m \ge 3$. Describe the moduli space $\mathcal{M}_m / \mathbb{Z}[1/m]$ of elliptic curves with level-$m$ structure, and compute the Galois group of the Drinfeld level-$p^n$ covering $\pi_n: \mathcal{M}_{\Gamma(p^n), m} \to \mathcal{M}_m$ as $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/p^n\mathbb{Z})$.
    - Compute the local Euler factor of the Hasse-Weil zeta function $\zeta_p(X, s)$ for a smooth projective variety $X / \mathbb{Q}$ with good reduction at $p$ via $\log \zeta_p(X, s) = \sum_{r=1}^\infty |\mathcal{X}(\mathbb{F}_{p^r})| \frac{p^{-r s}}{r}$.

