https://math.bme.hu/~gabor/oktatas/SztoM/TaoVu.AddComb.pdf, Tao-Vu additive combinatorics
    - (Page 2) Prove Markov's inequality: $\mathbb{P}(X \ge a) \le \frac{\mathbb{E}[X]}{a}$ for a non-negative random variable $X$.
    - (Page 3) Prove the Union Bound (Boole's inequality) using linearity of expectation on indicator functions: $\mathbb{P}(\bigcup E_i) \le \sum \mathbb{P}(E_i)$.
    - (Page 3) State and prove the Borel-Cantelli lemmas for sequences of events $(E_n)_{n \ge 1}$.
    - (Exercise 1.1.1) Compute Chebyshev's inequality $\mathbb{P}(|X - \mathbb{E}[X]| \ge \lambda \sigma) \le \frac{1}{\lambda^2}$ from Markov's inequality applied to $(X - \mathbb{E}[X])^2$.
    - (Theorem 1.8) Derive Chernoff bounds by applying Markov's inequality to the moment generating function $\mathbb{E}[e^{t X}]$.
    - State the Lovász Local Lemma (symmetric and asymmetric versions) for avoiding mutually dependent bad events.
    - (Lemma 2.1) Prove the sumset bounds $|A + B| \ge |A| + |B| - 1$ in $\mathbb{Z}$ and $|n A| \le \binom{|A| + n - 1}{n}$.
    - (Definition 2.5) Define the Ruzsa distance $d(A, B) = \ln \frac{|A - B|}{|A|^{1/2} |B|^{1/2}}$ and prove the Ruzsa triangle inequality $d(A, C) \le d(A, B) + d(B, C)$.
    - (Lemma 4.5) Define the discrete Fourier transform $\widehat{f}(\xi) = \mathbb{E}_{x \in G}[f(x) e(-\xi \cdot x)]$ on finite abelian groups and prove Parseval's and Plancherel's identities.

https://www.math.cmu.edu/~ttkocz/teaching/1819/read-sem-notes.pdf, Minkowski's theorem and lattice points
    - State Minkowski's Theorem: any symmetric convex body $C \subset \mathbb{R}^d$ with $\operatorname{vol}(C) > 2^d$ contains a non-zero lattice point in $\mathbb{Z}^d$.
    - Prove Fermat's Two-Square Theorem (primes $p \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ are sums of two squares) using Minkowski's theorem.

https://kskedlaya.org/cft/sec_Kummer_theory.html, Kummer theory
    - State and prove Hilbert's Theorem 90: $H^1(\operatorname{Gal}(L/K), L^\times) = 0$ for cyclic Galois extensions.
    - Formulate Kummer theory: abelian extensions of exponent $n$ of a field $K$ containing $\mu_n$ correspond bijectively to subgroups of $K^\times / (K^\times)^n$.

