https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247b.1.07w/notes9.pdf, Fourier analysis on finite abelian groups, Tao harmonic analysis
    - (Page 1) Define normalized Haar measure on a finite group $G$: $\int_G f(x) \, dx = \frac{1}{|G|} \sum_{x \in G} f(x)$.
    - (Page 3) State the Gelfand-Mazur theorem for finite abelian groups, showing that all irreducible translation-invariant subspaces are 1-dimensional.
    - (Page 5) State the Peter-Weyl theorem for finite abelian groups: the characters $\widehat{G}$ form an orthonormal basis of $L^2(G)$, yielding $f(x) = \sum_{\chi \in \widehat{G}} \widehat{f}(\chi) \chi(x)$.

https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247b.1.07w/notes10.pdf, representation theory for finite non-abelian groups, Tao harmonic analysis
    - (Page 2) Prove Weyl's unitary trick: every finite-dimensional representation of a finite group can be made unitary by averaging the inner product.
    - (Page 4) State Schur's Lemma for representations of finite groups over $\mathbb{C}$.
    - (Page 4) Prove the Jordan-Hölder and Maschke theorems: every representation of a finite group over $\mathbb{C}$ decomposes uniquely into a direct sum of irreducible representations.
    - (Page 6) Define the matrix-valued Fourier transform $\widehat{f}(\rho) = \int_G f(x) \rho(x)^* \, dx$ and prove the non-abelian Fourier inversion formula.

