https://www.math.brown.edu/~jhs/Presentations/WyomingEllipticCurve.pdf, elliptic curves Silverman slides
    - (Slide 9) Compute the discriminant $\Delta = -16(4A^3 + 27B^2)$ of the Weierstrass elliptic curve $y^2 = x^3 + Ax + B$.
    - (Slide 16) Describe the geometric chord-and-tangent group law on an elliptic curve.
    - (Slide 27) Derive the algebraic addition formulas for $P_1 + P_2 = P_3 = (x_3, y_3)$ using the slope $\lambda = \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$ (or $\lambda = \frac{3x_1^2 + A}{2y_1}$ if $P_1 = P_2$).
    - (Slide 41) Define the Weierstrass $\wp$-function $\wp(z; \Lambda) = \frac{1}{z^2} + \sum_{\omega \in \Lambda \setminus \{0\}} \left( \frac{1}{(z-\omega)^2} - \frac{1}{\omega^2} \right)$ and its differential equation $(\wp')^2 = 4\wp^3 - g_2\wp - g_3$.
    - (Slide 42) Show that $E(\mathbb{C}) \cong \mathbb{C}/\Lambda \cong S^1 \times S^1$, and compute its $N$-torsion subgroup $E[N] \cong \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$.
    - (Slide 43) State the Mordell-Weil Theorem: for an elliptic curve $E / \mathbb{Q}$, $E(\mathbb{Q}) \cong E(\mathbb{Q})_{\mathrm{tors}} \oplus \mathbb{Z}^r$.
    - (Slide 45) State Mazur's Torsion Theorem classifying the 15 possible torsion subgroups $E(\mathbb{Q})_{\mathrm{tors}}$.
    - (Slide 49) State Hasse's Theorem: for an elliptic curve over $\mathbb{F}_p$, $|E(\mathbb{F}_p) - (p + 1)| \le 2\sqrt{p}$.
    - (Slide 64) Define the Weil pairing $e_N: E[N] \times E[N] \to \mu_N$ as a non-degenerate, alternating, Galois-equivariant bilinear form.
    - (Slide 76) Define the logarithmic height $h(P) = \ln \max(|a|, |b|)$ for $x(P) = a/b \in \mathbb{Q}$, and the Néron-Tate canonical height $\widehat{h}(P) = \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{h(2^n P)}{4^n}$.
    - (Slide 93) State the Birch and Swinnerton-Dyer (BSD) Conjecture relating the algebraic rank of $E(\mathbb{Q})$ to the order of vanishing of $L(E, s)$ at $s = 1$.

