https://www.math.toronto.edu/~ila/Lang%20--%20Algebraic%20number%20theory.pdf, Lang's algebraic number theory
    - (Page 5) Define an element $x \in B$ to be integral over $A \subseteq B$ if $x$ satisfies a monic polynomial with coefficients in $A$.
    - (Page 6) Prove that the integral closure of $A$ in $B$ is a subring of $B$.
    - (Page 6) Prove that if $L/K$ is a finite separable field extension and $\alpha \in \mathcal{O}_L$, then $\operatorname{Tr}_{L/K}(\alpha) \in \mathcal{O}_K$ and $\operatorname{Nm}_{L/K}(\alpha) \in \mathcal{O}_K$.
    - (Page 8) State the Lying Over and Going Up theorems for integral extensions of commutative rings.
    - (Page 11) State the Chinese Remainder Theorem for pairwise comaximal ideals in a commutative ring: $A/\bigcap \mathfrak{a}_i \cong \prod A/\mathfrak{a}_i$.

