    - (Page 2) Define products and coproducts via their universal properties in a category $\mathcal{C}$.
    - (Page 7) Define kernels and cokernels in an additive/abelian category.
    - (Page 11) Define projective objects $P$ ($\operatorname{Hom}(P, -)$ is exact) and injective objects $I$ ($\operatorname{Hom}(-, I)$ is exact).
    - (Page 13) Prove that every abelian group embeds into an injective abelian group (divisible $\mathbb{Z}$-module).
    - (Page 21) Define chain complexes $(C_\bullet, d_\bullet)$ with $d^2 = 0$, chain maps, chain homotopies, and homology groups $H_n(C_\bullet) = \ker(d_n)/\operatorname{im}(d_{n+1})$.
    - (Page 28) State the Snake Lemma and construct the connecting homomorphism for the long exact sequence in homology.
    - (Page 36) Define left derived functors $L_n F(A) = H_n(F(P_\bullet))$ using projective resolutions, and right derived functors $R^n F(A) = H^n(F(I^\bullet))$ using injective resolutions.

