    - (Page 5) Define the 0-th Galois cohomology group $H^0(G, A) = A^G$ as the subgroup of $G$-invariants.
    - (Page 5) Define 1-cocycles $Z^1(G, A) = \{f: G \to A \mid f(\sigma \tau) = f(\sigma) + \sigma f(\tau)\}$ and 1-coboundaries $B^1(G, A) = \{f(\sigma) = \sigma a - a\}$, and compute $H^1(G, A) = Z^1(G, A) / B^1(G, A)$.

