https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/EOM95.pdf, Milne's definition of a Shimura variety in 2 pages
    - Define a Shimura variety as a double coset space $\operatorname{Sh}_K(G, X) = G(\mathbb{Q}) \backslash (X \times G(\mathbb{A}_f)) / K$ for a reductive group $G / \mathbb{Q}$, a symmetric domain $X$, and a compact open subgroup $K \subset G(\mathbb{A}_f)$.
    - State the Baily-Borel theorem: every Shimura variety has a canonical realization as a quasi-projective algebraic variety over $\mathbb{C}$ with a canonical model over its reflex field $E(G, X)$.

https://www.imo.universite-paris-saclay.fr/~francois.charles/TLDR9.pdf, local class field theory in 3 pages
    - Define the invariant map $\operatorname{inv}_K: \operatorname{Br}(K) \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}$ on the Brauer group of a non-archimedean local field $K$.
    - State the Local Artin Reciprocity Theorem: the local Artin map $\theta_K: K^\times \to \operatorname{Gal}(K^{\mathrm{ab}}/K)$ is an injective homomorphism with dense image, identifying $\mathcal{O}_K^\times \cong I_K^{\mathrm{ab}}$ and sending uniformizers $\pi_K$ to geometric Frobenius elements.

https://arxiv.org/pdf/1211.6357, Scholze's and Weinstein's notes of moduli of p-divisible groups

https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/1995IAS.pdf, Milne's expository articles on Shimura varieties
    - (Page 2) Define the local zeta function $Z_v(Y, T) = \exp\left(\sum_{m=1}^\infty N_m \frac{T^m}{m}\right)$ of a smooth projective variety $Y$ over a finite residue field $k(v)$, where $N_m = |Y(k(v)_m)|$.
    - (Page 3) Express the local zeta function via the characteristic polynomials of Frobenius on $\ell$-adic étale cohomology: $Z_v(Y, T) = \prod_{i=0}^{2\dim Y} P_i(T)^{(-1)^{i+1}}$ where $P_i(T) = \det(1 - T \cdot \operatorname{Frob}_v \mid H_{\text{ét}}^i(Y_{\overline{k}}, \mathbb{Q}_\ell))$.
    - (Page 4) Classify Hermitian symmetric domains $X = G(\mathbb{R}) / K$ and their associated simple Lie groups via Dynkin diagrams and special nodes.

https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/Tate100.pdf, arithmetic duality summary by Milne in 23 pages
    - (Page 2) Define the Weil-Châtelet group $\operatorname{WC}(A/K) \cong H^1(K, A)$ classifying principal homogeneous spaces (torsors) for an abelian variety $A / K$.
    - (Page 2) State the Tate Local Duality theorem: for an abelian variety $A$ over a local field $K$, the cup product pairing $H^1(K, A) \times A'(K) \to H^2(K, \mathbb{G}_m) \cong \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}$ is a perfect pairing of locally compact groups, where $A'$ is the dual abelian variety.
    - (Page 3) State the Barsotti-Weil formula: the dual abelian variety $A'$ represents the functor $\operatorname{Ext}^1(A, \mathbb{G}_m)$ of extensions of $A$ by $\mathbb{G}_m$.
    - (Page 4) Formulate the Poitou-Tate 9-term exact sequence of global arithmetic duality for Galois cohomology over number fields.

https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/MOT.pdf, motives in 15 pages summary by Milne
    - (Page 1) Formulate Poincaré duality and the Hard Lefschetz theorem on Betti cohomology of compact Kähler manifolds.
    - (Page 2) State the Weil Conjectures for smooth projective varieties over finite fields (rationality, functional equation, Riemann hypothesis, and Betti numbers) as proven by Dwork, Grothendieck, and Deligne.
    - (Page 3) Describe Grothendieck's category of pure Chow motives $\mathbf{Mot}(k)$ constructed from smooth projective varieties with correspondences modulo rational/algebraic/numerical equivalence.

https://example.com/davenport-multiplicative-number-theory, Davenport's Multiplicative Number Theory
    - (Page 2) Explain Euler's proof of the infinitude of primes using the divergence of the harmonic series via the Euler product $\zeta(s) = \prod_p (1 - p^{-s})^{-1}$ as $s \to 1^+$.
    - (Page 2) Describe Dirichlet's extension of Euler's proof to primes in arithmetic progressions $a \pmod q$ using Dirichlet $L$-functions $L(s, \chi) = \sum \chi(n) n^{-s}$ and showing $L(1, \chi) \ne 0$.

https://math.jhu.edu/~jmb/note/torext.pdf, Tor and Ext group computations
    - (Page 1) Compute the tensor products $\mathbb{Z} \otimes_\mathbb{Z} H \cong H$, $\mathbb{Q} \otimes_\mathbb{Z} \mathbb{Q} \cong \mathbb{Q}$, and $\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z} \otimes_\mathbb{Z} \mathbb{Z}/m\mathbb{Z} \cong \mathbb{Z}/\gcd(n, m)\mathbb{Z}$.
    - (Page 2) Compute $\operatorname{Tor}_1^\mathbb{Z}(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}, H) \cong H[n] = \{h \in H \mid n h = 0\}$, giving $\operatorname{Tor}_1^\mathbb{Z}(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}, \mathbb{Z}/m\mathbb{Z}) \cong \mathbb{Z}/\gcd(n, m)\mathbb{Z}$.
    - (Page 2) Prove that $\operatorname{Tor}_1^\mathbb{Z}(\mathbb{Z}, H) = 0$ and $\operatorname{Tor}_1^\mathbb{Z}(\mathbb{Q}, H) = 0$ since $\mathbb{Z}$ is projective and $\mathbb{Q}$ is a flat $\mathbb{Z}$-module.
    - (Page 4) Compute $\operatorname{Hom}_\mathbb{Z}(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}, H) \cong H[n]$ and $\operatorname{Ext}_\mathbb{Z}^1(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}, H) \cong H / n H$.
    - (Page 4) Compute $\operatorname{Ext}_\mathbb{Z}^1(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}, \mathbb{Z}) \cong \mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}$ and $\operatorname{Ext}_\mathbb{Z}^1(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}, \mathbb{Z}/m\mathbb{Z}) \cong \mathbb{Z}/\gcd(n, m)\mathbb{Z}$.
    - (Page 5) Compute $\operatorname{Hom}_\mathbb{Z}(\mathbb{Q}, \mathbb{Z}) = 0$ and $\operatorname{Ext}_\mathbb{Z}^1(\mathbb{Q}, \mathbb{Z}) \cong \mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}^\infty / \mathbb{Q} \cong \mathbb{R} \oplus \dots$, which is an uncountably infinite-dimensional $\mathbb{Q}$-vector space.

https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/svn.pdf, Shimura varieties in 3 pages
    - (Page 1) Classify simply connected 1-dimensional Riemann surfaces as the Riemann sphere $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{C})$, the complex plane $\mathbb{C}$, and the unit disk/upper half-plane $\mathbb{D} \cong \mathbb{H}$.
    - (Page 1) Construct Shimura curves as quotients $\Gamma \backslash \mathbb{H}$ where $\Gamma \subset B^\times$ is a discrete arithmetic subgroup arising from a quaternion algebra $B$ over a totally real field.
    - (Page 2) Define automorphic forms on Shimura curves and characterize their $q$-expansions and rationality properties over number fields.
    - (Page 3) Formulate Deligne's general axiomatic definition of Shimura varieties as algebraic moduli of abelian varieties with Hodge cycles.

