https://www.ams.org/notices/200301/what-is.pdf, What is a Shtuka? by David Goss
    - Explain the analogy between the differential operator $\frac{d}{dt}$ in characteristic zero and the Frobenius $p$-power operator $\tau(x) = x^p$ in characteristic $p$.
    - Define the non-commutative polynomial ring $L\{\tau\}$ over a field of characteristic $p$ satisfying the commutation relation $\tau \cdot c = c^p \cdot \tau$.
    - Define a Drinfeld $A$-module of rank $d$ over $L$ as an $\mathbb{F}_p$-algebra homomorphism $\psi: A \to L\{\tau\}$ such that $\psi_T = i(T) + a_1 \tau + \dots + a_d \tau^d$ with $a_d \ne 0$.
    - Define a Drinfeld shtuka of rank $d$ on a curve $X / \mathbb{F}_p$ as a diagram of vector bundles $\mathcal{E} \xrightarrow{j} \mathcal{E}' \xleftarrow{\tau} \mathcal{E}$ where $j$ and $\tau$ are sheaf morphisms with cokernels supported on the pole $\infty$ and zero (characteristic point).

https://www.ams.org/notices/200410/what-is.pdf, What is a Motive? by Barry Mazur
    - Explain how the Jacobian variety $J(C) = \operatorname{Pic}^0(C)$ linearizes a smooth projective curve $C$, providing the universal 1-dimensional abelian variety quotient for degree zero divisors.
    - Formulate Grothendieck's vision of motives as the universal cohomology theory factoring all classical Weil cohomology functors (Betti, de Rham, $\ell$-adic, crystalline) through an intermediate abelian category $\mathbf{Mot}(k)$.

https://arxiv.org/pdf/0904.4265, gerbes and Cheeger-Simons theory

https://www.ams.org/notices/200302/what-is.pdf, What is a Gerbe? by Nigel Hitchin
    - Describe line bundles via transition functions $g_{\alpha\beta} \in \mathcal{O}^*$ on double overlaps $U_\alpha \cap U_\beta$ satisfying the 1-cocycle condition $g_{\alpha\beta} g_{\beta\gamma} g_{\gamma\alpha} = 1$, classified by $H^1(M, \mathcal{O}^*)$.
    - Define a holomorphic gerbe via transition functions $g_{\alpha\beta\gamma} \in \mathcal{O}^*$ on triple overlaps $U_\alpha \cap U_\beta \cap U_\gamma$ satisfying the 2-cocycle condition $g_{\beta\gamma\delta} g_{\alpha\gamma\delta}^{-1} g_{\alpha\beta\delta} g_{\alpha\beta\gamma}^{-1} = 1$, classified by $H^2(M, \mathcal{O}^*)$.
    - Describe how a bundle of projective spaces $P \to M$ with structure group $\operatorname{PGL}_{n+1}(\mathbb{C})$ defines an obstruction class in $H^2(M, \mathcal{O}^*)$ to lifting to a vector bundle $\mathrm{GL}_{n+1}(\mathbb{C})$.
    - Define connective structures and curving on a gerbe to construct the 3-form curvature $H \in \Omega^3(M)$, representing a characteristic class in de Rham cohomology $[H/2\pi] \in H_{\mathrm{dR}}^3(M)$.
    - Connect gerbes to the Dixmier-Douady class in $H^3(M, \mathbb{Z})$ and twisted $K$-theory.

