https://simonsfoundation.s3.amazonaws.com/share/mps/conferences/2017_Conference_on_Number_Theory_Geometry_Moonshine_and_Strings/Kim.pdf, Arithmetic Chern-Simons theory by Minhyong Kim
    - (Slide 4) Define the spectrum $\operatorname{Spec}(A)$ as the topological space of prime ideals of $A$ equipped with the Zariski topology.
    - (Slide 24) Define the arithmetic zeta function $\zeta(X, s) = \prod_{x \in X_0} \frac{1}{1 - N(x)^{-s}}$ for an arithmetic scheme $X / \mathbb{Z}$.
    - (Slide 34) Define the étale fundamental group $\pi_1^{\text{ét}}(X, \bar{x}) = \varprojlim \operatorname{Aut}_X(Y)$ classifying finite étale coverings $Y \to X$.
    - (Slide 45) Prove that $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})$ is simply connected in the étale topology: $\pi_1^{\text{ét}}(\operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})) = 0$ (Minkowski's theorem on discriminants).

