https://www.ams.org/notices/200304/what-is.pdf, What is a Stack? by Barbara Fantechi
    - Explain why the coarse moduli space of elliptic curves $\mathcal{M}_{1, 1} \cong \mathbb{A}^1$ (via the $j$-invariant) fails to admit a universal family: elliptic curves possess non-trivial automorphisms ($\pm \operatorname{id}$), preventing fine moduli spaces of schemes.
    - Define the moduli stack of elliptic curves $\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$ as a category fibered in groupoids over $\mathbf{Sch}$ where objects over $S$ are smooth proper families of elliptic curves $E \to S$, capturing all automorphism groups.

https://www.ams.org/notices/201107/rtx110700955p.pdf, What is a Derived Stack? by Bertrand Toën
    - Explain why classical moduli spaces and intersection theory fail for non-transverse intersections, motivating derived algebraic geometry.
    - Define derived schemes and derived stacks as functors from simplicial commutative rings (or $\mathbb{E}_\infty$-rings) to simplicial sets ($\infty$-groupoids), replacing the classical truncation with homotopically smooth derived moduli spaces.

https://www.ams.org/notices/200307/what-is.pdf, What is a Dessin d'Enfant? by Leila Schneps
    - Define a Grothendieck dessin d'enfant as a bipartite graph embedded in a compact oriented topological surface whose complement is a union of topological disks.
    - State Belyi's Theorem: a smooth projective algebraic curve $X / \mathbb{C}$ is defined over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ if and only if there exists a non-constant meromorphic function $\beta: X \to \mathbb{P}^1$ (a Belyi map) ramified at most over $\{0, 1, \infty\}$.
    - Explain how the absolute Galois group $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ acts faithfully on dessins d'enfants.

https://www.ams.org/notices/200805/tx080500586p.pdf, What is a Toric Variety? by David Cox
    - Define an affine toric variety $X_\sigma = \operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{C}[S_\sigma])$ from a strongly convex rational polyhedral cone $\sigma \subset N_\mathbb{R}$, and a general toric variety $X_\Sigma$ from a fan $\Sigma$.
    - Connect projective toric varieties to lattice polyhedra $P$ and moment maps $\mu: X_P \to P$ in symplectic geometry with fiber $T^n = (S^1)^n$.

