https://ymsc.tsinghua.edu.cn/__local/7/B5/04/0890A5CE2893D5380292FD983CD_99A1AD7E_31656.pdf, pedagogical introduction to p-adic Hodge theory
    - (Page 1) Recall the classical Hodge decomposition for a smooth projective variety $X / \mathbb{C}$: $H^n(X, \mathbb{C}) \cong \bigoplus_{p+q=n} H^{p, q}(X)$.
    - (Page 2) Define the $p$-adic valuation $v_p: \mathbb{Q}_p \to \mathbb{Z} \cup \{\infty\}$ and the field $\mathbb{C}_p = \widehat{\overline{\mathbb{Q}_p}}$ as the completion of the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_p$.
    - (Page 2) State the Hodge-Tate comparison theorem: for a smooth projective variety $X / K$, $H_{\text{ét}}^n(X_{\overline{K}}, \mathbb{Q}_p) \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}_p} \mathbb{C}_p \cong \bigoplus_{p+q=n} H^q(X, \Omega_{X/K}^p) \otimes_K \mathbb{C}_p(-p)$.

