https://swc-math.github.io/aws/2020/2020KimNotes1.pdf, Selmer schemes and non-abelian Chabauty
    - Explain the geometric classification of Diophantine equations by genus: genus 0 (rational points via the Hasse principle), genus 1 (elliptic curves via Mordell-Weil $E(\mathbb{Q}) \cong E(\mathbb{Q})_{\mathrm{tors}} \oplus \mathbb{Z}^r$ and BSD), and genus $g \ge 2$ (Faltings' theorem: $X(\mathbb{Q})$ is finite).
    - Define arithmetic principal $U$-bundles over $\operatorname{Spec}(K)$ for a topological group $U$ with continuous $G_K$-action, classified by the non-abelian Galois cohomology set $H^1(G_K, U)$.
    - Describe the non-abelian Chabauty method (Chabauty-Kim) constructing the unipotent Albanese map $j: X(\mathbb{Q}) \to H^1(G_\mathbb{Q}, U)$ into the Selmer variety $\operatorname{Sel}(U)$ and intersecting with local $p$-adic points $X(\mathbb{Q}_p) \hookrightarrow H^1(G_{\mathbb{Q}_p}, U)$.

https://swc-math.github.io/aws/2020/2020KimLecture2Slides.pdf, Kim-Chabauty Slide 2
    - Explain the necessity of base points in universal covering spaces to obtain universal categorical properties and define fiber functors $F_x: \mathbf{Cov}(X) \to \mathbf{Set}$.

https://swc-math.github.io/aws/2020/2020KimLecture4Slides.pdf, Kim-Chabauty Slide 4
